1
00:03:53,076 --> 00:03:59,076
The war's not over until the last man comes home.

2
00:07:46,153 --> 00:07:52,153
Missing in Action is a action, adventure, thriller film directed by Joseph Zito.

3
00:11:39,230 --> 00:11:45,230
American servicemen are still being held captive in Vietnam and it's up to one man to bring them home in
this blistering, fast-paced action/adventure starring martial arts superstar Chuck Norris.

4
00:15:32,307 --> 00:15:38,307
Following a daring escape from a Vietnamese POW camp, Special Forces Colonel James
Braddock (Norris) is on a mission to locate and save remaining MIAs.

5
00:19:25,384 --> 00:19:31,384
Col. James Braddock, played by Chuck Norris.

6
00:23:18,461 --> 00:23:24,461
Tuck, played by M. Emmet Walsh.

7
00:27:11,538 --> 00:27:17,538
Sen. Porter, played by David Tress.

8
00:31:04,615 --> 00:31:10,615
Ann, played by Lenore Kasdorf.

9
00:34:57,692 --> 00:35:03,692
Gen. Trau, played by James Hong.

10
00:38:50,769 --> 00:38:56,769
Jacques, played by Pierrino Mascarino.

11
00:42:43,846 --> 00:42:49,846
Missing in Action is a 1984 American action film directed
by Joseph Zito and starring Chuck Norris.

12
00:46:36,923 --> 00:46:42,923
It is set in the context of the Vietnam War POW/MIA issue.

13
00:50:30,000 --> 00:50:36,000
Colonel Braddock, who escaped a Vietnamese prisoner of war camp ten years earlier, returns to
Vietnam to find American soldiers listed as missing in action during the Vietnam War.

14
00:54:23,076 --> 00:54:29,076
The film was followed by a prequel, Missing in Action 2: The Beginning (1985), and a sequel, Braddock:
Missing in Action III (1988), it is the first installment in the Missing in Action film series.

15
00:58:16,153 --> 00:58:22,153
The first two Missing in Action installments had been filmed back-to-back with the intent to have the
first film involve the POW years of Braddock (as directed by Lance Hool) be the first film.

16
01:02:09,230 --> 01:02:15,230
However, it was determined that the commercial prospects were stronger
with the film directed by Zito involving the POW rescue.

17
01:06:02,307 --> 01:06:08,307
As such, Hool's film was turned into Missing in Action 2 and labeled as a
prequel that detailed events before those in Missing in Action.

18
01:09:55,384 --> 01:10:01,384
It is the first of a series of films themed around the Vietnam War POW/MIA issue that were produced by Menahem Golan and Yoram
Globus and released under their Cannon Films banner, with whom Norris would have a long professional relationship.

19
01:13:48,461 --> 01:13:54,461
Norris later dedicated these films to his younger brother Wieland.

20
01:17:41,538 --> 01:17:47,538
Wieland, a private in the 101st Airborne Division, had been killed in June 1970
in Vietnam while on patrol in the defense of Firebase Ripcord.

21
01:21:34,615 --> 01:21:40,615
The film, however, was criticized heavily as being a preemptive cash-in on the Rambo franchise, with both the
first and second Missing in Action films being released just months before the second Rambo film.

22
01:25:27,692 --> 01:25:33,692
Despite the overwhelmingly negative reception from critics, the film was a
commercial success and has become one of Chuck Norris's most popular films.

23
01:29:20,769 --> 01:29:26,769
It was also Chuck Norris's first film with The Cannon Group.

24
01:33:13,846 --> 01:33:19,846
The film explores themes of vietnam war, vietnam
veteran, martial arts, vietnam, patriotism.

25
01:37:06,923 --> 01:37:12,923
The tone is emotional and intense.
